//monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Cinder_Beetle_Armor_Quests\">Cinder Beetle Armor Quests</a> (Hult Beetlewrangler, <a href=\"/zones/night-harbor.html\">Night Harbor</a>, min lvl 1)</li><li><b>Range:</b> <a class=\"itm q-common\" data-i=\"Krindor&#x27;s Hunting Bow\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Krindor%27s_Hunting_Bow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Krindor&#x27;s Hunting Bow</a> <span class=\"dim\">(lvl 6)</span> — Vendor: Archery Supplies; Night Harbor<br><span class=\"up\">by 10 →</span> <a class=\"itm q-magic\" data-i=\"Bow of the Fallen Ranger\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Bow_of_the_Fallen_Ranger\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bow of the Fallen Ranger</a> <span class=\"dim\">(lvl 10)</span> — Named drop: Dario Numas (lvl 10) — <a href=\"/zones/tomb-of-the-last-wyrmsbane.html\">Tomb of the Last Wyrmsbane</a>, -</li></ul></div><div class=\"qi-sec\"><h3>Where to level 6–10 <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span></h3><ul class=\"tight\"><li><a href=\"/zones/blind-midden.html\">Blind Midden</a> <span class=\"dim\">(zone lvl ?; 33 listed camps in band)</span></li><li><a href=\"/zones/ailvorith.html\">Ail&#x27;Vorith</a> <span class=\"dim\">(zone lvl 1 - 50; 28 listed camps in band)</span></li><li><a href=\"/zones/evershade-weald.html\">Evershade Weald</a> <span class=\"dim\">(zone lvl 1 - ??; 22 listed camps in band)</span></li><li><a href=\"/zones/sungreet-strand.html\">Sungreet Strand</a> <span class=\"dim\">(zone lvl ?; 11 listed camps in band)</span></li><li><a href=\"/zones/tomb-of-the-last-wyrmsbane.html\">Tomb of the Last Wyrmsbane</a> <span class=\"dim\">(zone lvl 3-15; 10 listed camps in band)</span></li><li><a href=\"/zones/underdocks.html\">Underdocks</a> <span class=\"dim\">(zone lvl 1 - 50; 9 listed camps in band)</span></li><li><a href=\"/zones/keepers-bight.html\">Keeper&#x27;s Bight</a> <span class=\"dim\">(zone lvl 5 - ??; 6 listed camps in band)</span></li></ul><p class=\"src\">Zones whose wiki mob tables overlap the band. Full camp lists: <a href=\"/leveling.html\">Leveling by band</a>.</p></div><div class=\"qi-sec\"><h3>Tips</h3><p><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Official class page — defining traits:</p><ul class=\"tight\"><li>Light-armored melee DPS</li><li>Harnesses magical force across telekinetic, electric, and arcane schools</li><li>Shifts between different weapon infusions, each with its own damage type and proc effects</li><li>Manages infusion cooldowns as a primary combat cycle</li><li>Conduit discharges the active infusion for a powerful burst at the cost of a cooldown</li><li>Can place stationary arcane fields and explosive zones that damage enemies within range</li><li>Can teleport behind a target and strike, or blink away from melee range when pressed</li><li>Uses telekinetic effects including knockback, root, and enemy repositioning</li></ul><details><summary>What the devs say is changing</summary><p>Updates to the Spellblade are about focus and depth: fewer schools of magic, more expression within the ones that remain. Elemental magic is going away in favor of arcane, telekinetic, and electric schools that fit the class more naturally, and the one-off pet is being removed.</p><p>The infusion and conduit system is the heart of the combat experience, and the ability suite around it is being built out to give the Spellblade a more interesting and varied damage rotation. Spell lines are getting better progression and scaling across the full level range, and teleportation is being treated as a genuine combat mechanic rather than a utility footnote.</p><p><b>More:</b> Focus on the infusion and conduit system as the core combat cycle; Teleportation as a central combat mechanic; Arcane field and damage zone tools; Depth and scaling across the full level range</p><p><b>Less:</b> Elemental magic; Off-tank focus; Generic caster utility</p></details><p><b>Group:</b> Infusions, damage fields (deep dive); Kick back at L3 (0.30.2.1).</p><p><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> <b>Duo partners:</b> <a href=\"/classes/fighter.html\">Fighter</a>, <a href=\"/classes/shadow-knight.html\">Shadow Knight</a>, <a href=\"/classes/paladin.html\">Paladin</a>, <a href=\"/shaman/index.html\">Shaman</a> — chosen to cover what Spellblade lacks (Melee DPS).</p><p><a href=\"/classes/spellblade.html\">Full Spellblade guide →</a></p></div>","Spellblade|11-15":"<div class=\"qi-sec\"><h3>Class at a glance <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span></h3><table class=\"kv\"><tr><th>Archetype</th><td>Highly-Mobile Magic Swordsman</td></tr><tr><th>Roles</th><td>Melee DPS</td></tr><tr><th>Armor</th><td>Leather (wiki)</td></tr><tr><th>Weapons</th><td>Staves, daggers, scythes, swords (wiki)</td></tr><tr><th>Races (official)</th><td>Deep Dwarf, Deep Elf, Dwarf, Gnome, High Elf, Human</td></tr><tr><th>Class stat modifier</th><td>+2 STR, +3 DEX, +3 INT.</td></tr><tr><th>Main stat</th><td><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"qi-sec\"><h3>Spells &amp; abilities 11–15 <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span></h3><ul class=\"tight\"><li><b>L11 Lesser Spellshield</b> <span class=\"dim\">(Vendor)</span> — A magical shield encircles you, increasing your HP by 25, AC by 10, and Magic Resistance by 10.</li><li><b>L12 Arcane Spear II</b> <span class=\"dim\">(Vendor)</span> — Hurl a spear of arcane energy at your target, dealing 30 to 112 Magic Damage. While Arcane Infusion is…</li><li><b>L12 Kinetic Ward II</b> <span class=\"dim\">(Vendor)</span> — Construct a kinetic ward, increasing your Armor Class by 10 and absorbing 75 melee damage for 5 seconds.…</li><li><b>L14 Seclusion</b> <span class=\"dim\">(Vendor)</span> — Secludes your target, reducing your Threat against them by 100 (L1) to 100 (L40), immobilizing them, and…</li></ul><p class=\"src\">Wiki <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Spellblade\">Spellblade</a> rev 69767. Wiki levels can lag patches.</p></div><div class=\"qi-sec\"><h3>Gear to equip 11–15 <span class=\"badge fact\">items: fact</span> <span class=\"badge strat\">pick: strategy</span></h3><p class=\"dim\">What to wear per slot when you enter the band, and the upgrade to grab by level 15. Items and sources are from the wiki (quest, vendor, craft or drop — no auction needed). Hover an item for its stats.</p><ul class=\"tight gearlist\"><li><b>Head:</b> <a class=\"itm q-magic\" data-i=\"Cinder Beetle Helm\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Cinder_Beetle_Helm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cinder Beetle Helm</a> <span class=\"dim\">(lvl 1)</span> — Quest: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Cinder_Beetle_Armor_Quests\">Cinder Beetle Armor Quests</a> (Hult Beetlewrangler, <a href=\"/zones/night-harbor.html\">Night Harbor</a>, min lvl 1)</li><li><b>Face:</b> <a class=\"itm q-magic\" data-i=\"Firesnout Mask\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Firesnout_Mask\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Firesnout Mask</a> <span class=\"dim\">(lvl 7)</span> — Named drop: Grantha Scrigglehex (lvl 7) — <a href=\"/zones/sungreet-strand.html\">Sungreet Strand</a>, Outside Tel Ekir<br><span class=\"up\">by 15 →</span> <a class=\"itm q-common\" data-i=\"Pristine Scarab Mask\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Pristine_Scarab_Mask\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Pristine Scarab Mask</a> <span class=\"dim\">(lvl 13)</span> — Named drop: a pristine beetle (lvl 13), Crypt (Day)</li><li><b>Ear:</b> <a class=\"itm q-magic\" data-i=\"Wyrmsbane Grandmaster&#x27;s Earring\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Wyrmsbane_Grandmaster%27s_Earring\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wyrmsbane Grandmaster&#x27;s Earring</a> <span class=\"dim\">(lvl 10)</span> — Named drop: Grandmaster Gildas (lvl 10) — <a href=\"/zones/tomb-of-the-last-wyrmsbane.html\">Tomb